    "created_at": "2026-01-04T17:02:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T17:02:48Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the great question! Yes your observation is accurate, in current implementation the \"aug_entropy_loss\" does not directly affect the gradients; the major regularization should come from the entropy on pi_theta; empirically we did find that adding this aug_entropy_loss slightly improves performance which we are not entirely sure on the reason (may be due to some numerical stability); \nIn order to make the aug_entropy_loss affect the gradients I believe we need to do an additional forward on the masked sequence during the actor updating steps; we haven't try this setting but would be interesting to see results! Thanks!",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
