    "created_at": "2026-01-30T16:27:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-30T16:27:31Z",
    "body": "Hi! We did a few additional experiments and would like to share with you some results from our investigation. We tried adding an additional forward on the masked sequence during the policy update, and recompute the aug_log_probs for the aug entropy loss. We considered three settings under this change: (1) aug entropy only; (2) double entropy, and (3) double entropy with a lowered eta (since the regularization on gradient should be stronger with the recomputed aug probs); PS. The code will be updated in `workers/actor/dp_actor.py` with a switch `RECOMPUTE_AUG_LOG_PROBS`, which you can use for turn on the additional forward pass. \n\n\nThe results are as follows. We find that adding the additional forward generally results in slightly lower or similar performance compared to our original version. The training time will be longer due to additional inference. And we still need a relatively large eta, e.g., 0.05, as when we lower eta the performance start to drop.\n\n\n| Model (Qwen2.5-VL-7B) | Geo3K | MathVista | We-Math | MMK12 | MathVerse | LogicVista | Counting | MMMU-Pro | MathVerse-V | AVG\n|-|-|-|-|-|-|-|-|-|-|-|\n|**(original) no additional forward on aug probs**|\n| PAPO-G w/ Single Ent (eta=0.05) | 41.49 | 66.71 | 67.59 | 71.76 | 69.13 | 44.46 | 88.63 | 35.91 | 64.43 | 61.12\n| PAPO-G w/ Double Ent (eta=0.05) | 40.25 | 69.53 | 66.79 | 72.52 | 68.43 | 46.07 | 89.81 | 36.63 | 64.97 | **61.66**\n||\n|**add additional forward on aug probs**|\n| PAPO-G w/ Single Aug Ent (eta=0.05) | 40.95 | 67.03 | 68.62 | 72.79 | 68.02 | 46.59 | 87.94 | 35.02 | 64.08 | 61.23\n| PAPO-G w/ Double Ent (eta=0.05) | 40.20 | 66.68 | 69.25 | 73.84 | 68.22 | 46.73 | 87.25 | 35.35 | 64.14 | 61.30\n| PAPO-G w/ Double Ent (eta=0.02) | 38.71 | 65.84 | 65.85 | 73.45 | 66.44 | 46.13 | 92.31 | 35.51 | 64.27 | 60.95\n\nHope this investigation provides more context; and thanks again for the insightful discussion!",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
